31. kill
Stop a process using its PID.

Example:

kill 900
This normally sends:

SIGTERM
SIGTERM asks the application to terminate gracefully.

Force Kill
kill -9 900
This sends:

SIGKILL
The kernel immediately terminates the process.

Use kill -9 only when necessary because the application cannot perform normal cleanup.

You do NOT always need to be root.

You can generally signal:

Your own processes
Root or appropriate privileges are required to signal processes owned by other users.

